ued donating money from  each paycheck  to the special operations warrior  foundation the nonprofit funds  education for all children who lose a  parent serving in special operations  from preschool through college even  knowing that  his cancer journey would ultimately  likely come to this result  you know it wasn't on our radar that our  family would be covered by it my husband  my best friend  our hero in may at just 41 years old  ron lost his three-year battle against  cancer  what most people don't really take into  account i think  is that family behind ron  miranda tyler and cameron they're  serving as well  clay huttmacher is the president of the  special operations warrior foundation  the foundation was started in the  aftermath of the failed rescue attempt  for the 52 hostages held in tehran  we lost eight americans three marines  five air force that left behind 17 kids  the survivors of that mission made a  commitment  at that time to take care of the  education of those 17 kids  we've had a nearly 1500 children in our  program since 1980 and  there's 908 right now that are in the  program that we've committed to funding  the special operations warrior  foundation recently expanded their  program  to include medal of honor families like  the shores and you know the really cool  thing is  our mentors are graduates from our  program  like ebony cheryl whose father major  jeffrey sherrill  a special forces doctor was killed in  1996  when she was just four years old he just  wanted us  to not have money  get in the way of us living out our  dream  was there a point um in high school or  maybe middle school  where you weren't sure your family could  afford college  yeah but my dad wanted so badly for us  to get an education and  i really wanted to do that for my family  so that we can  just turn our lives around and and just  get to a better place  cheryl reached out to the special  operations warrior foundation for  assistance  when they said okay everything